CM ============================================================
CM  VHF/UHF REMOTE ELEMENT SWITCHING SYSTEM
CM  ANTENNA: 3-ELEMENT REVERSIBLE YAGI, 6 METERS (50.1 MHz)
CM  TYPE: SYMMETRIC - BEAM REVERSAL BY ELEMENT ROLE SWAP
CM
CM  CONCEPT: Both outer elements are IDENTICAL in length.
CM  When FORWARD: element at -Y acts as reflector (shorted),
CM    element at +Y acts as director (open).
CM  When REVERSED: relay swaps roles - element at +Y becomes
CM    reflector, element at -Y becomes director. Driven
CM    element remains at center.
CM
CM  ELEMENT DATA (all dimensions in meters):
CM    Outer Element A: L = 2.914 m  pos Y = -1.346 m
CM    Driven Element:  L = 2.842 m  pos Y =  0.000 m
CM    Outer Element B: L = 2.914 m  pos Y = +1.346 m
CM
CM  OUTER ELEMENT LENGTH: Compromise between reflector (0.494λ)
CM    and director (0.449λ) = 0.4715λ × 1.05 = 0.487λ = 2.914 m
CM    This provides ~8 dB F/B in either direction.
CM
CM  ELEMENT DIAMETER: 12.7 mm (1/2 in. aluminum tube)
CM  BOOM HEIGHT AGL:  10.0 m
CM  EXPECTED GAIN FWD:  5.5 dBd (7.65 dBi) - reduced vs asymmetric
CM  EXPECTED F/B:       8-10 dB
CM
CM  FORWARD STATE (beam toward +Y):
CM    Tag 1 (A): relay shorts element to boom (reflector)
CM    Tag 3 (B): relay opens element (director)
CM  REVERSE STATE (beam toward -Y):
CM    Tag 1 (A): relay opens element (director)
CM    Tag 3 (B): relay shorts element to boom (reflector)
CM
CM  NOTE: This model shows FORWARD state. For REVERSE,
CM    swap roles of tags 1 and 3 in relay controller.
CE
GW 1 11 -1.457 -1.346 10.000 1.457 -1.346 10.000 0.00635
GW 2 11 -1.421 0.000 10.000 1.421 0.000 10.000 0.00635
GW 3 11 -1.457 1.346 10.000 1.457 1.346 10.000 0.00635
GE 0
GN 2 0 0 0 13.0 0.005
EX 0 2 6 0 1.0 0.0
FR 0 5 0 0 50.0 0.1
RP 0 361 1 1000 0.0 0.0 1.0 0.0
RP 0 1 361 1000 90.0 0.0 0.0 1.0
EN
